  "warnings": [
    "Enemy LEFT/RIGHT naming is inconsistent: PREPPY uses base/'r'; WHITE uses base/'1' (1 = RIGHT); SHADY uses '1'/'r' (1 = LEFT). Wire textures from the velX>=0 mapping in Enemy.java to avoid flipping variants.",
    "player.png, banana.png, rb.png are NOT referenced in any Java file directly — they are passed as strings from caller code (scene/state). Treat as in-use by semantics.",
    "Gorilla frames are individual PNGs with non-uniform dimensions; Java re-decodes the PNG every tick. Phaser should preload all four and use setTexture/setOrigin(0.5).",
    "ImageGameObject loads PNGs on every render for directional/animated swaps — port must preload, never re-decode at runtime.",
    "BombExplosion uses e*.png (despite the b/e prefix muddle). SpaceShipThrust uses ONLY b14-b16. 17 other b*.png files are dead weight.",
    "Animation frames are non-uniform in size in both sequences — pack with a trim-aware atlas (TexturePacker JSON) rather than a fixed-grid spritesheet.",
    "Legacy canvas anchor is top-left; Phaser default origin is 0.5. Either setOrigin(0,0) or recenter to (0.5,0.5) and adjust positions consistently.",
    "blackhole.png is 2.6MB at 1230x1264 — downscale before shipping to web.",
    "back.jpg is 1.9MB at 1920x1080 — consider WebP/AVIF.",
    "Sentry DSN is hard-coded in strings.xml — strip or rotate before shipping a public web build.",
    "ic_launcher and ic_launcher_round are byte-identical per DPI bucket — dedupe.",
    "ic_launcher_foreground.xml is the stock Android robot, not Galaxy Monkey branding — regenerate from title.png or a fresh mark for PWA.",
    "rotate.xml is a generic 16s linear infinite spin View animation — unrelated to e/b sequences."
  ],

